{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Cu1zdDeyLqmcfYhdjmgL4F","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"2025 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewers in 2024\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12056528/\"},{\"title\":\"Can LLM feedback enhance review quality? A randomized study of 20K   reviews at ICLR 2025\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2504.09737\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2023 and CoRL 2024 reviewer guidelines, but not specific information for CoRL 2025. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2024 Review Criteria\n\nCoRL submissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\n## CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines\n\nThe CoRL 2023 guidelines emphasize several important principles:\n\n- CoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, and reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly and with high appreciation.\n\n- Obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and be strongly reflected in scores.\n\n- Reviewers should be constructive and concrete, courteous and respectful, start with positive aspects, and suggest improvements.\n\nUnfortunately, I couldn't find specific scoring criteria or the detailed review form structure for CoRL 2025. For the most current and detailed information about CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines, I recommend visiting the official CoRL 2025 website directly, as the search results returned guidelines from previous years and other conferences (NeurIPS and ICLR).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"937facd1-3ff3-4809-b45a-58cd38966ef5","uuid":"a2813162-9192-41d1-81a2-56c157f26899","timestamp":"2026-05-20T17:06:19.929Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Y9A5bZsD1KgAHpcERqsa4u","content":[{"title":"2025 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"Reviewers in 2024","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12056528/"},{"title":"Can LLM feedback enhance review quality? A randomized study of 20K   reviews at ICLR 2025","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2504.09737"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2023 and CoRL 2024 reviewer guidelines, but not specific information for CoRL 2025. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2024 Review Criteria\n\nCoRL submissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\n## CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines\n\nThe CoRL 2023 guidelines emphasize several important principles:\n\n- CoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, and reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly and with high appreciation.\n\n- Obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and be strongly reflected in scores.\n\n- Reviewers should be constructive and concrete, courteous and respectful, start with positive aspects, and suggest improvements.\n\nUnfortunately, I couldn't find specific scoring criteria or the detailed review form structure for CoRL 2025. For the most current and detailed information about CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines, I recommend visiting the official CoRL 2025 website directly, as the search results returned guidelines from previous years and other conferences (NeurIPS and ICLR)."],"durationSeconds":5.300935591000001}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0171KSXsk6RpdBfG4twAYyAa","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2026, though a dedicated CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines page with a specific review form wasn't directly located. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Reviewer Information\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer. They are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ ICRA/ IROS/ RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/ NeurIPS/ ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\nThe search results indicate that CoRL has a history of detailed reviewer guidelines. For reference, the review criteria typically assess whether the paper addresses a problem in robot learning, applies or improves a learning-based method, is evaluated in simulation or on real robots, and would interest the CoRL audience.\n\n## How to Access the Review Form\n\nThe actual review form and complete reviewer guidelines for CoRL 2026 would be available on the OpenReview platform. Papers are submitted through OpenReview via the link at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference. The review form and detailed guidelines would typically be accessible to invited reviewers through their OpenReview accounts.\n\nFor the most current and detailed CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, I recommend checking the CoRL website directly or accessing your OpenReview account if you've been invited to review.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"937facd1-3ff3-4809-b45a-58cd38966ef5","uuid":"ff7ee974-b947-4bad-8fb2-7e7c4b6fc30a","timestamp":"2026-05-20T17:06:21.134Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01TXtCx3nWpDsc3AQAW1KBHo","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers","url":"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2026, though a dedicated CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines page with a specific review form wasn't directly located. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Reviewer Information\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer. They are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ ICRA/ IROS/ RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/ NeurIPS/ ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\nThe search results indicate that CoRL has a history of detailed reviewer guidelines. For reference, the review criteria typically assess whether the paper addresses a problem in robot learning, applies or improves a learning-based method, is evaluated in simulation or on real robots, and would interest the CoRL audience.\n\n## How to Access the Review Form\n\nThe actual review form and complete reviewer guidelines for CoRL 2026 would be available on the OpenReview platform. Papers are submitted through OpenReview via the link at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference. The review form and detailed guidelines would typically be accessible to invited reviewers through their OpenReview accounts.\n\nFor the most current and detailed CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, I recommend checking the CoRL website directly or accessing your OpenReview account if you've been invited to review."],"durationSeconds":6.635439678999999}}
