{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012bzVGeHJJWWyv4LcbqYrJq","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines scoring rubric acceptance criteria review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2023-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"ACL’23 Peer Review Form - ACL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/review-form/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2023-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"Best Reviewers Award for 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10957073/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewers in 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10965321/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/\"}]\n\nI found information about CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines. Based on the search results, here's what I found:\n\n## Reviewer Guidelines\n\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section. Reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly with high appreciation, while obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and strongly reflected in scores.\n\nReviewers should be constructive and concrete; be courteous and respectful; start with positive aspects and suggest improvements; and make reviews as informative and substantiated as possible.\n\nThe guidelines also provide examples of reviewer mistakes to avoid, noting that claims like \"This is not novel\" or \"This has been done before\" should be supported with citations to prior work, and alternative suggestions should include evidence rather than just opinions.\n\nThe search results point to the official CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines page at corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines, which would have the complete scoring rubric and acceptance criteria. However, the specific scoring scale and detailed acceptance criteria weren't fully displayed in the search results I retrieved.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"937facd1-3ff3-4809-b45a-58cd38966ef5","uuid":"b6e07955-f0e5-40df-96e5-b2338b0c9cf8","timestamp":"2026-05-20T17:06:34.117Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines scoring rubric acceptance criteria review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01FLJzMi7ukJBF7PoGeyNMHb","content":[{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2023 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2023-statistics/"},{"title":"ACL’23 Peer Review Form - ACL 2023","url":"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/review-form/"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2023 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2023-paper-list/"},{"title":"Best Reviewers Award for 2023","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10957073/"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"Reviewers in 2023","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10965321/"},{"title":"CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/"}]},"I found information about CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines. Based on the search results, here's what I found:\n\n## Reviewer Guidelines\n\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section. Reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly with high appreciation, while obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and strongly reflected in scores.\n\nReviewers should be constructive and concrete; be courteous and respectful; start with positive aspects and suggest improvements; and make reviews as informative and substantiated as possible.\n\nThe guidelines also provide examples of reviewer mistakes to avoid, noting that claims like \"This is not novel\" or \"This has been done before\" should be supported with citations to prior work, and alternative suggestions should include evidence rather than just opinions.\n\nThe search results point to the official CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines page at corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines, which would have the complete scoring rubric and acceptance criteria. However, the specific scoring scale and detailed acceptance criteria weren't fully displayed in the search results I retrieved."],"durationSeconds":5.865160532999998}}
